00:07:52.598 --> 00:07:58.598
The show also recaps recent space news, including NASA's Artemis Acceleration Plans and International

00:07:58.598 --> 00:08:05.410
Satellite Network developments. Danish astronomer Tyco Brahe died in Prague on October 24th,

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:11.590
1601. After constructing large quadrants, an armillary sphere, a sextant, and a large

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:16.470
globe for precise pre-telloscopic observations, astronomy magazine recounts.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:22.670
He ranks second only to Galileo in a 2022 astronomy magazine list of the 20 greatest astronomers.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:30.210
Brahe measured the 1572 Supernova and the great comet of 1577, finding no parallax and

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.090
placing both objects beyond the moon.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:37.950
His meticulous stellar and planetary position data passed to Johannes Kepler, enabling the

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:42.410
derivation of the laws of planetary motion that later underpinned Isaac Newton's work.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:47.510
Brahe had discovered early in his career that existing published positions were grossly

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:52.150
inaccurate and devoted his life to correcting them through sustained instrumental measurements.

